+/// by forming a `&Instance` / `&ComponentInstance`: on exactly the path this
+/// guard detects, the owning thread may hold `&mut` to that allocation, so
+/// materializing a shared reference to it is itself the aliasing violation
+/// the guard exists to report. Both store-context slots sit at
+/// shape-independent constant offsets, so this costs nothing.
+///
